horizon forbidden west is the  long-awaited sequel to horizon zero dawn  we'll once again be following humanity's  champion eloy as she journeys toward the  wreckage of the american west coast to  try and save the world here's everything  you need to know about horizon forbidden  west  set six months after the events of  horizon zero dawn the world is ending  again between deranged machines fierce  storms and a blight ripping through the  planet and destroying its crops the  remaining humans are struggling to get  by  eloy a former outcast needs to get to  the bottom of what's going on by heading  to the forbidden west gathering allies  and exploring the remains of earth to  help uncover the secrets that will save  it on her journey she'll travel to new  areas like san francisco and las vegas  as well as meet new tribes like the  uttaru farmers who work the dying land  and the tanakh a tribe driven by war and  combat and try and make them work  together to try and save the world  it's not as simple as just making nice  though as a rebel tanakh tribe will  cause problems for everyone and a  greater threat looms over them all  ashley burch and lance riddick reprise  their roles as nora outcast eloy and the  mysterious silence who seems to have his  own plans and joining the cast are  angela bassett playing tanakh rebel  regala and carrie anne moss who plays a  mysterious character called tilde if you  want to get caught up on the story  before forbidden west make sure to  subscribe we've got a full story recap  coming your way and believe me you'll  need it  horizon forbidden west aims to build on  what came before in horizon zero dawn  with similar mechanics and combat but  gorilla is expanding on elo's suite of  abilities and equipment to show that  she's a more competent and experienced  fighter than she was in the first game  at the same time the studio has said  that it wants to keep her abilities  relatively realistic and human ailoy  obtains a pull caster for traversal that  allows her to grapple onto points around  the world and while she can climb more  freely and even wall jump now she's  still a human and will struggle with  particularly steep inclines the  polecaster also acts as a winch meaning  you'll be able to use it to rip open  vents to create more paths for you to  travel she can also swim underwater  thanks to a new diving mask and as in  the first game aloy can override  machines to ride around the world in  forbidden west she's able to use even  more machine types as mounts to make  getting down as fun as going up she can  use the shield wing a new item that acts  as a glider to help get around the map  totally new to the game is the workbench  where eloi can put her crafting skills  to good use to upgrade her outfit and  weapons which can then be customized  with mod slots as well as unlockable  perks you'll be able to equip outfits  and gear with passive stat boosts and  perks which when coupled with the new  skills in the redesigned skill tree  should help you prepare for anything the  forbidden west might throw at you combat  has also seen some tweaks with gorilla  wanting to encourage player choice and  experimentation when they find  themselves up against the ferocious  metal beasts that roam the forbidden  west the machines have gotten their own  upgrades with an emphasis on better ai  and traversal tools that will let them  jump climb swim and look for shortcuts  to head you off ailoy is not the only  person who can ride machines either  you'll be coming up against other  factions who can use the machines as  mounts there are also new machines that  you'll come up against like the  ginormous tremor tusk who looks and acts  like a giant war elephant there's also  the rollerback the pterodactyl-esque sun  wing and the giant slitherfang  snakes why's it always gotta be snakes  when you encounter enemies you'll be  able to sneak away but enemies will  remember where they saw you and start to  search if you're not where they expected  to find you there are also new  unlockable abilities called valor surges  they will absolutely help you out if  things get a little bit hairy these new  skills have three levels and can be  powered up by removing components on  enemies or by hitting their weak points  the higher the level of your valor surge  the more damage you'll deal missions can  consist of contracts to complete certain  types of tasks like gathering a  particular material from fallen machines  and of course the return of ruins and  cauldrons forbidden west will also  include a new warrior arena that will  test your combat skills  horizon forbidden west will be available  on both playstation 4 and playstation 5.  more on that in a second but as of the  writing of this video it's not confirmed  for pc we think it's a safe bet to say  it may come to pc eventually as  playstation has started to put first  party games like day's gone god of war  and of course the original horizon onto  the platform in a recent sony blog q a  interview playstation boss hermann hulst  asserted that the company intends to  further invest in the pc space though  most of the game has been shown on ps5 a  set of ps4 screens released by gorilla  shows the game looking awfully nice on  that platform as well given that horizon  zero dawn was among the more stunning  games for the ps4 gorilla may be able to  push the hardware to its limit and make  it an impressive showpiece there too  speaking to game informer the game's  director has tried to assuage fears  about the ps4 version he said a lot of  the development has taken place on the  playstation 4 and a lot of play testing  is also done on playstation 4. so we are  ensuring that owners of that console  will have a great experience and that  the game will look fantastic well let's  hope so gorilla has detailed some of the  upgrades we can expect to see on the  playstation 5 version such as the  mapping of accurate facial expressions  and body movements but the studio says  that the playstation 4 version is not  compromised on ps5 you'll also get all  the advantages of sony's shiny new  console like faster load times thanks to  the high speed solid state drive and  targeted 60 frames per second in  performance mode the game will also make  use of the dual sense controller's  haptic feedback as you journey and fight  through the world as well as the  resistance on the adaptive triggers  making you feel like you're actually  drawing the string on your bow it'll  also make use of the ps5's tempest 3d  audio tech  [Music]  so far no dlc or microtransactions have  been announced for forbidden west you  might remember that zero dawn did get a  meaty dlc expansion called the frozen  wilds which opened up a new snowy region  to explore and introduce new factions  hopefully gorilla will do something  similar for forbidden west and will  obviously have all the news if it  happens  forbidden west was originally set for  launch in 2021 but slipped into early  2022 that delay actually had an  unexpected impact on its price sony had  previously announced that all games in  the ps5 launch window would receive a  free upgrade from the ps4 to ps5  versions but as horizon slipped outside  this window that deal wasn't valid  anymore after fan outcry sony quickly  reversed its decision meaning that if  you buy forbidden west on ps4 for 60  dollars you can upgrade to the ps5  version for free seems like a great deal  to me as the ps5 version by itself costs  70  if you want all the bells and whistles  including digital soundtrack art book  comic and extra in-game resources like  weapons and outfits as well as photo  mode extras then the digital deluxe  edition for ps4 and 5 will set you back  80 bucks  we have a ton of horizon content on the  horizon  like graphics comparisons tips  walkthroughs and of course our review so  make sure you like this video and  subscribe so you don't miss out thanks  for watching  [Music]
 

